<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>John-the-Apostle on John, Complected</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/tags/john-the-apostle/</link><description>Recent content in John-the-Apostle on John, Complected</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><copyright>© 2026</copyright><lastBuildDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://john-nicholson.github.io/tags/john-the-apostle/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Remember Who You Are — Greater Is He Who Is in You</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-greater-is-he-who-is-in-you/</link><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-greater-is-he-who-is-in-you/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1&amp;#43;John&amp;#43;4%3A4%E2%80%9318&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;1 John 4:4–18&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Read alongside: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm&amp;#43;56&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Psalm 56&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Fear can be very convincing. It can make a thought feel certain simply because it feels strong. It can make something small feel enormous, or make us feel that because we are frightened, the thing we fear must have power over us.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;John writes to believers with a very different perspective:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1&amp;#43;John&amp;#43;4%3A4&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;1 John 4:4&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;That is not a promise that frightening things will never happen. It is a reminder about &lt;strong&gt;who is greater&lt;/strong&gt;. Fear is not greater. Confusion is not greater. The things we cannot explain are not greater. &lt;strong&gt;Jesus is greater.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>